# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values.
# `.env.local` is gitignored; this example file is the only one committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# IMPORTANT — what NEXT_PUBLIC_ actually means:
# Next.js inlines every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value into the browser bundle at build
# time. These are PUBLIC CONFIG, not secrets. They stay out of the git repo,
# but visitors (and scrapers) can still read them on the deployed site.
# Never put an API key, token, or password behind a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# Every value below has a working fallback in data/portfolio.ts, so the site
# builds and runs correctly even with no .env.local present.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Contact email shown in the hero, contact cards, and mailto: links.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Where every "Resume" button points. Use a path under /public, or an external
# link (Google Drive, Dropbox) if you would rather not commit the PDF.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RESUME_URL=/resumes/YOUR_RESUME.pdf

# Public profile links.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_URL=https://github.com/your-handle
NEXT_PUBLIC_LINKEDIN_URL=https://linkedin.com/in/your-handle
